strings |id, value|

bug_descriptions |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_negative_z_index_parsed_positive_2026-11-28, 0, "z-index parses without its sign: declarations.spl:820 calls parse_int (simple_web_html_layout_renderer_foundation_values.spl:1025), which skips a leading '-', so z-index:-5 becomes 5. Every negative z-index box then opens a positive stacking context and paints on top. Probe: two absolute siblings, the first z-index:-5 #aa0000 at x 0..49, the second z-index:2 #00aa00 at x 20..69; Simple paints x 30 red, Chrome 159 green."
    web_render_negative_z_index_parsed_positive_2026-11-28, 1, "Same root: a z-index:-1 absolute backdrop in a position:relative flex (or plain block) container paints over the in-flow item. Chrome 159 (k=1, column 20): G 0..19 over Y 20..29; Simple: Y 0..29 on base 0829e113e88 and on work/webrender-float-paint-order-20261128. The Draw IR order also has no negative-z step (CSS 2.2 Appendix E Step 3): with the sign kept, a z<0 positioned box becomes a Step 4 block in tree order."

bugs_active |id, severity, status, title, file, line, reproducible_by, created_at, updated_at, valid|
    web_render_negative_z_index_parsed_positive_2026-11-28, P2, fix-implemented-verification-pending, "web render: a negative z-index is parsed as positive and paints on top", src/lib/gc_async_mut/gpu/browser_engine/simple_web_html_layout_renderer_declarations.spl, 820, "<div style='position:absolute;z-index:-5;left:0;top:0;width:50px;height:20px;background:#aa0000'></div><div style='position:absolute;z-index:2;left:20px;top:0;width:50px;height:20px;background:#00aa00'></div>; read x 30", 2026-11-28, 2026-11-28, true

bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    web_render_negative_z_index_parsed_positive_2026-11-28, 0, "2026-11-28 float-paint-order lane: found, not fixed (style parsing, outside the paint-order lane; a fix moves every page with a negative z-index and needs a negative-z step in _html_draw_ir_emit_scope). One file under examples/06_io/ui/web_catalog and test/01_unit/browser_engine uses z-index:-. The lane's flex/grid item test excludes absolute/fixed children, which is unreachable until this is fixed; pin it with a Chrome case then."
    web_render_negative_z_index_parsed_positive_2026-11-28, 1, "2026-11-28 negz lane (work/webrender-negative-z-index-20261128): z-index parses with its sign (parse_signed_leading_int at declarations.spl and decl_apply.spl; parse_int unchanged, no other caller affected). Every positioned box opens a Draw IR context; z<0 children paint after the context root (document: #root, html, body when its bg is the canvas one) and before in-flow blocks. Spec test/01_unit/browser_engine/negative_z_index_paint_order_chrome159_spec.spl red 0/5 on base 1f1ebb62124, green 8/8 (AC-6 1x catalog entry; AC-7/AC-8 an opacity body/html with a negative-z child is emitted once, double emission caught in review and fixed). The flex/grid is_item absolute guard stays unreachable by construction (every absolute/fixed box opens a context); the spec pins the behaviour, not the line."
    web_render_negative_z_index_parsed_positive_2026-11-28, 2, "Follow-ups, not fixed: (b) a z-index:auto positioned parent still opens a z=0 Draw IR context (pre-existing), so its negative child paints over the parent's background instead of under the parent context's in-flow content. (c) a context root's deferred outline flushes before its negative children; Chrome paints outlines at Step 10. (d) opacity<1 is a sub-scope, not a stacking context: with body{opacity:.5} plus a z-index:-1 box Chrome 159 paints the box inside the group (k=1 column 50: #7ed47e 0..19, #d47e7e 20..39), Simple paints it opaque under the group."

